   "gap": "Supply this exact entry's hypotheses: the entry never states its observation space (or restricts the contaminating law H), yet its exact claim sup_{R in H_1} E_R N_{a,b} = E_{Q_1} N_{a,b} = (1-(3/5)^r)/(2/5) and the annex argument (annex lines 486-514: 'its mass p at one ranges over [2/5,3/5]'; 'If no such observation has occurred by time r, the test exits at the lower boundary') hold only when the space is {0,1}. Under def:p15-sequential-endpoint-setting (arbitrary measurable observation space, H any probability) and the clipped-score convention of thm:p15-huber-contamination-pair (r=1 on the common null set, so l(x)=(4/5)max{3/4,min(infinity,1)}=4/5 there), R=(4/5)P_1+(1/5)delta_x with x outside {0,1} lies in H_1 and at a=3c gives P_R(N>3)=19/125>0=P_{Q_1}(N>3), hence E_R N >= 264/125 > 49/25 = E_{Q_1} N. The failure condition 'unstated assumption' therefore holds. Owed: state X={0,1} (or restrict H to laws on {0,1}) as a hypothesis of the entry, or compute and prove the worst-case expected size over the full stated alternative class."
  }
